# Vendored third-party builds are stored byte-for-byte as shipped: no line-ending
# translation, and no diffs in review (they are minified, so a diff is noise).
vendor/** -text -diff

# ── GIT LFS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Canva source artwork and the photo transport archive go through LFS rather
# than straight into history. Two reasons, and only the first is a preference:
#
#   1. "FINAL STYLIST CARD.pdf" is 109,989,428 bytes. GitHub's hard per-file
#      limit is 104,857,600, so a normal push of that file is REJECTED — not
#      warned about, rejected. LFS is what makes it pushable at all.
#   2. ~162MB of binaries in ordinary history is 162MB every clone pays for
#      forever, even though none of it is served by the live site.
#
# The whole of _source/ is tracked, not just the two big files, so anything
# dropped in there later (a re-drawn card, a new head icon) is handled without
# editing this file. Anyone cloning needs git-lfs installed; without it they get
# small pointer files instead of the artwork, which is harmless for the site but
# confusing if you don't know to expect it.
_source/** filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
stylist/photos.zip filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
